      "excerpt": "We had one customer, a distributor, whose revenue accounted for approximately 15% and 12% of our total revenue for the quarters ended October 2, 2026 and October 3, 2025, respectively, across all reportable segments. Revenue from PSG Revenue from PSG increased by $152.3 million, or approximately 21%, for the quarter ended October 2, 2026 compared to the quarter ended October 3, 2025 due to higher demand. This was driven by an increase in revenue of $64.9 million, $71.3 million and $31.4 million in the industrial, AI data center and other end-markets, respectively, offset by a decrease of $15.3 million within the automotive end-market. Revenue from AMG Revenue from AMG increased by $14.0 million, or approximately 2%, for the quarter ended October 2, 2026 compared to the quarter ended October 3, 2025, primarily driven by an increase of $18.4 million and $43.3 million in the automotive and AI data center end-markets, respectively, due to higher demand, offset by a decrease of $41.6 million and $6.1 million within the industrial and other end-markets, respectively. Revenue from ISG Revenue from ISG increased by $5.1 million, or approximately 2%, for the quarter ended October 2, 2026 compared to the quarter ended October 3, 2025 due to increased demand. This was driven by an increase in revenue of $17.2 million and $1.6 million in the industrial and other end-markets, respectively, offset by a decrease of $13.7 million in the automotive end-market. 33 Table of Contents Revenue by Geographic Location Revenue by geographic location, based on sales billed from the respective country or region, was as follows (dollars in millions): Quarter Ended October 2, 2026 As a % of Total Revenue (1) Quarter Ended October 3, 2025 As a % of Total Revenue (1) Hong Kong $ 567.8 33.0 % $ 424.9 27.4 % Singapore 436.9 25.4 % 320.1 20.6 % United Kingdom 316.7 18.4 % 315.0 20.3 % United States 294.3 17.1 % 340.5 22.0 % Other 106.6 6.2 % 150.4 9.7 % Total revenue $ 1,722.3 $ 1,550.9 (1) Certain amounts may not total due to rounding of individual amounts. Gross Profit and Gross Margin Gross profit increased by $125.8 million, or approximately 21%, to $713.0 million for the quarter ended October 2, 2026 compared to $587.2 million for the quarter ended October 3, 2025 primarily due to higher revenue, improved manufacturing utilization and favorable product mix within certain business segments, partially offset by higher prices for certain manufacturing inputs. Our gross margin increased by 3.5 percentage points from 37.9% for the quarter ended October 3, 2025 to 41.4% for the quarter ended October 2, 2026.",
